---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security Architecture"
  description="How Retenqo secures APK distribution, browser headers, and vulnerability reporting."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p
      class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-primary)] uppercase"
    >
      Security
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Security Architecture
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      This website is engineered as a minimal-attack-surface static distribution
      platform. The design follows the principle of least privilege: no backend,
      no user accounts, no server-side state.
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          Verified APK Distribution
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          All APK downloads point directly to official GitHub Releases for{' '}
          <a
            href={SITE_CONFIG.appRepoUrl}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent-primary)] underline"
          >
            {SITE_CONFIG.appRepoUrl.replace('https://github.com/', '')}
          </a>
          . Release metadata is schema-validated at build time, and SHA-256 checksums
          plus signing certificate fingerprints are published for independent verification.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          Android data protection
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Retenqo encrypts its Room database with SQLCipher. A randomly
          generated database passphrase is encrypted by an AES-GCM key held in
          Android Keystore. The app migrates an existing plaintext Room database
          before opening it and fails closed if the protected key is unavailable
          rather than replacing the data.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Pending notification queue contents and ordinary preferences are
          currently app-private but not application-encrypted. Notification
          sources start paused and are user-selectable; screen context,
          microphone, and file access require explicit Android permission or
          user-selected files. Revoked notification sources are removed from the
          pending queue before processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          Backup protection
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          New backup exports use a password-derived AES-256-GCM key. The app
          does not save the password. Legacy JSON backups may be imported and
          are not encrypted; handle them as plaintext. Keep backup passwords and
          exported files under your control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          Zero-Backend Attack Surface
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          No database, no user accounts, no server-side sessions, and no
          third-party tracking scripts. Strict HTTP security headers (HSTS,
          X-Frame-Options: DENY, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff,
          Referrer-Policy: no-referrer) are enforced at the edge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          Vulnerability Reporting
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you discover a security issue in the website or Android
          application, please report it responsibly to{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}`}
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent-primary)] underline"
          >
            {SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}
          </a>
          . See also{' '}
          <a
            href="/.well-known/security.txt"
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent-primary)] underline"
          >
            security.txt
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
